<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Coal Sept qtr profits advance.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Coal Sept qtr profits advance.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Sept versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending	 20.59 vs 17.17</p>
<p>    Capital spending				  8.53 vs 4.40</p>
<p>    Sales						78.36 vs 62.79</p>
<p>    Cost of sales				    59.58 vs 46.22</p>
<p>    Coal produced (tonnes)		   2,323,000 vs 2,285,000</p>
<p>    Coal sold (tonnes)			 2,333,000 vs 2,157,000</p>
<p>Full name: Gold Fields Coal Ltd, part of Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - The quarter ended with over 300,000 tonnes on the stockpile as a shortage of trains and industrial unrest at the Richard's Bay terminal impacted negatively on sales.</p>
<p>Prices were strong, both locally and overseas.</p>
<p>Work is continuing on the feasibility study into the mining of 4-seam and 1-seam once the 2 and 5 seams are depleted. The company said results had been encouraging and the study was on target for presentation to the board at the end of the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
